  "source": {
    "template": "CAP Ampulla of Vater protocol v4.3.0.0, June 2025 (required use March 2026); QMH Cancer Reporting Template GI-Ampulla of Vater",
    "url": "https://www.cap.org/wp-content/uploads/documents/New-Cancer-Protocols-June-2025/Ampulla_4.3.0.0.REL_CAPCP.pdf",
    "staging": "AJCC 8th edition pTNM derived by src/staging/ampulla.js from the tumour-extension ticks. Tumour size never enters pT in this chapter. pT1a is limited to the ampulla or sphincter of Oddi; pT1b is perisphincteric invasion and/or duodenal submucosa; pT2 is duodenal muscularis propria; pT3a is pancreatic invasion of 0.5 cm or less; pT3b is pancreatic invasion over 0.5 cm, or peripancreatic/periduodenal soft tissue or duodenal serosa; pT4 is coeliac axis, superior mesenteric artery or common hepatic artery. pN1 is 1 to 3 involved nodes, pN2 is 4 or more. pTNM prints only with the printPTNM option, stamped (AJCC 8th edition). Treatment effect maps to the y descriptor automatically.",
    "stagingProtocol": "ampulla",
    "grading": "WHO 2019 digestive tumours histologic type and grade, with the pancreaticobiliary versus intestinal subtype distinction supported by CK7, CK20, CDX2, MUC1 and MUC2. Depth of pancreatic invasion is in cm because the pT3a/pT3b threshold is stated in cm; margin distances are in mm. Margins at 1 mm or less are reported as positive (R1).",
    "staging_reference": "https://digital.nhs.uk/ndrs/data/cancer-data-training-materials/staging-sheets/ampulla-of-vater"
  },
